Gateway ordinary reply loss: remove shard-wide permanent transition pause
2026-09-08

Changes:
- Removed transitionsPaused and its management status field.
- Ordinary unknown replies release admission accounting, without replay or
  preventing later preparation reservations on the same/different key.
- Valid dirty resumes do not pause new preparation.
- An already reserved operation waiting on an unknown request remains protected
  locally. Durable operation recovery, identity checks and cold validation remain.
- Preparation is NOT hot deletion authority. No automatic deletion introduced.

Local targeted race, three rounds:
go test -race ./internal/gateway \
  -run 'TestAdmissionRun|TestKeyBarrier|TestGuarded|TestBatch|TestDrainAndDeadline|TestHotPreparation' \
  -count=3
PASS gateway 6.589s
Includes fake RESP backend executing INCR once and dropping its reply, followed
by successful new preparation + mocked confirmation for the same/different key.
Actual Service listeners execute new preparation after a dirty boot; recovered
durable operation still blocks only its protected business key.

Related package race:
go test -race ./internal/gateway ./internal/syncer ./cmd/syncer
PASS gateway 38.777s; syncer and cmd/syncer cached.

Full local regression:
go test ./...
PASS gateway 37.815s, server 62.821s; remaining packages passed/cached/no tests.
go vet ./internal/gateway ./internal/syncer ./cmd/syncer: PASS.
git diff --check: PASS.

Additional real Redis test (added after the above regression):
Redis server v=7.2.5, local /opt/homebrew/bin/redis-server.
GATEWAY_TEST_REDIS_SERVER=/opt/homebrew/bin/redis-server \
  go test -race ./internal/gateway -run '^TestHotPreparationRedis' -count=3 -v
TestHotPreparationRedis: PASS 0.12s / 0.06s / 0.06s
TestHotPreparationRedisLostReply: PASS 0.07s / 0.07s / 0.07s
PASS gateway 2.726s
Each case starts its own loopback Redis in a test temporary directory.
Lost-reply relay forwards the command to real Redis and discards the executed
INCR reply; subsequent GET=42 and fresh preparation succeeds without manual reset.
The prepared business key stays protected; unavailable cold confirmation is
rejected and hot data is retained. No real Kvrocks in these additional tests.
Test fixture shuts down its own Redis with NOSAVE and joins the process.

No deployment, remote host changes, commit or push in this adjustment.
This does not implement automatic recovery of all pending operation barriers,
late-writer fencing, hot deletion, Cluster migration, or full Redis semantics.
